# Conventional Commits — https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
#
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Types:  feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
# Scopes: readme, pt-br, site, scripts, data, feeds, ci, deps (optional)
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period, 72 characters max.
#
# Body (optional): what changed and why, wrapped at 72 columns.
# Leave a blank line between the subject and the body.
#
# Footer (optional): BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Closes #123, Refs #123
#
# Examples:
#   feat(readme): add QuTiP to the quantum computing section
#   fix(pt-br): correct the SciX description
#   docs: document the release checklist
#   ci: validate commit messages in pull requests
